          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "sâbun is usually traced to Arabic ṣābūn, \"soap\" (Lane), and Persian still spells it with the Arabic ṣ. The word goes back to Latin sāpō, which the Romans took from a Germanic word, the ancestor of English soap. EtymDB also lists a Middle Persian sābōn."
